PASS R2c Owner edit clears a historical stuck create (needs_attention creation_unconfirmed)
PASS R2d Cancelling a visit whose only create failed in transit ends as cancelled, with no event
PASS R2e Cancel just after a create that commits 150 s late: no absence is counted before the create settles (M3)
PASS R2f Cancel path needs two absent reads at least 2 minutes apart (M5)
PASS R2g A re-POST stopped before sending restores the earlier dispatched marker and its absence reads (M10)
PASS R2h An unconfirmed create older than a week is not re-sent automatically; the owner is told, and an owner edit sends it again
PASS R7 Already seen, then deleted in Google with no tombstone left: an edit never re-creates it, with or without a receipt (M11 guard)
PASS R3 After a switch to another Google account, undelivered changes for old-calendar events are counted and explained
PASS R3b Account-switch attention clears once the affected visit date has passed (D2)
PASS R3c Control: platform-side attention on the current calendar stays the platform's to act on
PASS R4 Reconnect to the same calendar spends no Google requests on a past synced visit
PASS R4b Reconnect with no change to the visit keeps the owner's own edits in Google
PASS R5 DST spring-forward wall times resolve to the first instant after the gap and keep order
PASS R6 A visit cancelled while disconnected is flagged, then deleted after reconnecting the same account
